#%PAM-1.0
# Tilo session-unlock PAM stack.
#
# Used by `tilo-unlock-helper`, which the compositor spawns to verify the
# logged-in user's credential while the session is LOCKED. The helper only
# runs the auth + account phases (pam_authenticate + pam_acct_mgmt) — it never
# opens a session or starts a login — so this stack deliberately defines no
# session/password phases.
#
# It mirrors the greetd auth/account phases so an unlock accepts the same
# factors a login does: fingerprint (pam_fprintd) and systemd-homed are each
# offered as a *sufficient* factor and short-circuit to success on a match;
# otherwise PAM falls through to the distro's maintained `password-auth` stack
# (pam_unix). The leading "-" makes a factor a silent no-op when its module is
# absent, so this file ships safely whether or not fingerprint / homed support
# is installed.
-auth      sufficient   pam_fprintd.so
-auth      sufficient   pam_systemd_home.so
auth       substack     password-auth

-account   sufficient   pam_systemd_home.so
account    include      password-auth
